WEBVTT

00:00.620 --> 00:01.820
Mark 15

00:01.820 --> 00:04.720
And as soon as it was morning,

00:05.200 --> 00:06.780
the chief priests held a consultation

00:06.780 --> 00:09.900
with the elders and scribes and the whole council.

00:10.500 --> 00:12.720
And they bound Jesus and led him away

00:12.720 --> 00:14.480
and delivered him over to Pilate.

00:14.720 --> 00:15.960
And Pilate asked him,

00:16.300 --> 00:18.360
Are you the king of the Jews?

00:18.960 --> 00:20.460
And he answered him,

00:21.140 --> 00:22.400
You have said so.

00:23.060 --> 00:25.580
And the chief priests accused him of many things.

00:25.980 --> 00:27.400
And Pilate again asked him,

00:27.880 --> 00:29.740
Have you no answer to make?

00:30.220 --> 00:32.580
See how many charges they bring against you.

00:33.320 --> 00:35.220
But Jesus made no further answer,

00:35.520 --> 00:37.080
so that Pilate was amazed.

00:38.000 --> 00:39.280
Now at the feast,

00:39.460 --> 00:42.500
he used to release for them one prisoner for whom they asked.

00:42.900 --> 00:44.440
And among the rebels in prison

00:44.440 --> 00:46.620
who had committed murder in the insurrection,

00:47.220 --> 00:48.780
there was a man called Barabbas.

00:49.160 --> 00:51.680
And the crowd came up and began to ask Pilate

00:51.680 --> 00:53.200
to do as he usually did for them.

00:53.580 --> 00:54.960
And he answered them, saying,

00:55.760 --> 00:59.420
Do you want me to release for you the king of the Jews?

01:00.000 --> 01:02.100
For he perceived that it was out of envy

01:02.100 --> 01:04.160
that the chief priests had delivered him up.

01:04.860 --> 01:06.840
But the chief priests stirred up the crowd

01:06.840 --> 01:09.180
to have him release for them Barabbas instead.

01:09.880 --> 01:11.500
And Pilate again said to them,

01:12.200 --> 01:16.020
Then what shall I do with the man you call the king of the Jews?

01:16.920 --> 01:18.160
And they cried out again,

01:18.320 --> 01:20.320
Crucify him!

01:20.860 --> 01:22.440
And Pilate said to them,

01:22.920 --> 01:26.480
Woe! What evil has he done?

01:27.120 --> 01:28.660
But they shouted all the more,

01:29.340 --> 01:29.980
Crucify him!

01:30.000 --> 01:31.260
Crucify him!

01:31.860 --> 01:34.680
So Pilate, wishing to satisfy the crowd,

01:35.100 --> 01:36.520
released for them Barabbas,

01:36.740 --> 01:38.140
and having scourged Jesus,

01:38.540 --> 01:40.300
he delivered him to be crucified.

01:41.040 --> 01:43.660
And the soldiers led him away inside the palace,

01:43.880 --> 01:45.480
that is, the governor's headquarters.

01:46.060 --> 01:48.160
And they called together the whole battalion,

01:48.700 --> 01:50.720
and they clothed him in a purple cloak,

01:50.840 --> 01:52.720
and twisting together a crown of thorns,

01:52.980 --> 01:53.960
they put it on him,

01:54.260 --> 01:55.900
and they began to salute him.

01:58.100 --> 01:59.900
Hail, king of the Jews!

02:00.000 --> 02:03.240
And they were striking his head with a reed,

02:03.340 --> 02:04.220
and spitting on him,

02:04.320 --> 02:06.060
and kneeling down in homage to him.

02:06.720 --> 02:07.980
And when they had mocked him,

02:08.240 --> 02:09.840
they stripped him of the purple cloak,

02:09.980 --> 02:11.460
and put his own clothes on him.

02:11.940 --> 02:14.280
And they led him out to crucify him.

02:14.980 --> 02:16.880
And they compelled a passerby,

02:17.160 --> 02:18.140
Simon of Cyrene,

02:18.400 --> 02:19.920
who was coming in from the country,

02:20.140 --> 02:21.680
the father of Alexander and Rufus,

02:21.880 --> 02:23.180
to carry his cross.

02:24.200 --> 02:26.560
And they brought him to the place called Golgotha,

02:26.720 --> 02:28.200
which means place of a skull.

02:28.760 --> 02:29.860
And they offered him one of the most precious things in the world,

02:29.860 --> 02:31.100
wine mixed with myrrh,

02:31.200 --> 02:32.380
but he did not take it.

02:32.880 --> 02:34.180
And they crucified him,

02:34.420 --> 02:36.220
and divided his garments among them,

02:36.420 --> 02:37.560
casting lots for them,

02:37.860 --> 02:39.620
to decide what each should take.

02:40.460 --> 02:43.000
And it was the third hour when they crucified him.

02:43.580 --> 02:46.160
And the inscription of the charge against him read,

02:46.580 --> 02:48.120
The king of the Jews.

02:48.860 --> 02:51.040
And with him they crucified two robbers,

02:51.220 --> 02:53.000
one on his right and one on his left.

02:53.580 --> 02:55.520
And those who passed by derided him,

02:55.880 --> 02:57.280
wagging their heads and saying,

02:58.120 --> 02:58.720
Aha!

02:59.860 --> 03:03.120
You, who would destroy the temple

03:03.120 --> 03:05.760
and rebuild it in three days,

03:06.100 --> 03:09.860
save yourself and come down from the cross.

03:10.800 --> 03:13.160
So also the chief priests with the scribes

03:13.160 --> 03:14.860
mocked him to one another, saying,

03:15.680 --> 03:17.720
He saved others.

03:18.000 --> 03:19.380
He could not save himself.

03:19.880 --> 03:22.020
Let the Christ, the king of Israel,

03:22.180 --> 03:24.000
come down now from the cross

03:24.000 --> 03:26.200
that we may see and believe.

03:27.040 --> 03:29.100
Those who were crucified with him

03:29.100 --> 03:29.840
also replied,

03:29.860 --> 03:33.420
And when the sixth hour had come,

03:33.820 --> 03:35.780
there was darkness over the whole land

03:35.780 --> 03:37.020
until the ninth hour.

03:37.680 --> 03:38.820
And at the ninth hour,

03:38.980 --> 03:41.000
Jesus cried with a loud voice,

03:41.900 --> 03:57.100
Which means,

03:59.860 --> 04:01.340
My God,

04:02.180 --> 04:04.400
My God,

04:05.020 --> 04:10.640
Why have you forsaken me?

04:11.900 --> 04:14.420
And some of the bystanders hearing it said,

04:15.120 --> 04:16.780
Behold, he is calling Elijah.

04:17.340 --> 04:20.460
And someone ran and filled a sponge with sour wine,

04:20.860 --> 04:23.420
put it on a reed and gave it to him to drink, saying,

04:23.800 --> 04:27.700
Ah, wait, let us see whether Elijah will come to take him down.

04:28.480 --> 04:29.620
And Jesus uttered a loud voice,

04:29.620 --> 04:31.720
a loud cry and breathed his last.

04:32.520 --> 04:34.820
And the curtain of the temple was torn in two

04:34.820 --> 04:36.100
from top to bottom.

04:36.840 --> 04:39.000
And when the centurion who stood facing him

04:39.000 --> 04:41.600
saw that in this way he breathed his last,

04:41.840 --> 04:42.340
he said,

04:43.020 --> 04:45.860
Truly, this man was the Son of God.

04:46.840 --> 04:49.740
There were also women looking on from a distance,

04:49.980 --> 04:51.620
among whom were Mary Magdalene

04:51.620 --> 04:53.980
and Mary, the mother of James the Younger

04:53.980 --> 04:55.720
and of Joses, and Salome.

04:56.360 --> 04:57.720
When he was in Galilee,

04:57.720 --> 04:59.600
they followed him and ministered to him.

04:59.620 --> 05:01.720
And there were also many other women

05:01.720 --> 05:03.440
who came up with him to Jerusalem.

05:05.360 --> 05:06.940
And when evening had come,

05:07.120 --> 05:08.600
since it was the day of preparation,

05:09.120 --> 05:10.620
that is, the day before the Sabbath,

05:11.260 --> 05:12.680
Joseph of Arimathea,

05:12.900 --> 05:14.520
a respected member of the council

05:14.520 --> 05:17.080
who was also himself looking for the kingdom of God,

05:17.480 --> 05:19.080
took courage and went to Pilate

05:19.080 --> 05:20.660
and asked for the body of Jesus.

05:21.500 --> 05:22.920
Pilate was surprised to hear

05:22.920 --> 05:24.460
that he should have already died,

05:24.840 --> 05:26.320
and summoning the centurion,

05:26.320 --> 05:28.480
he asked him whether he was already dead.

05:29.620 --> 05:31.280
And when he learned from the centurion

05:31.280 --> 05:32.220
that he was dead,

05:32.480 --> 05:34.100
he granted the corpse to Joseph.

05:35.240 --> 05:37.260
And Joseph bought a linen shroud

05:37.260 --> 05:38.620
and taking him down,

05:39.440 --> 05:40.960
wrapped him in the linen shroud

05:40.960 --> 05:42.400
and laid him in a tomb

05:42.400 --> 05:44.100
that had been cut out of the rock.

05:45.200 --> 05:46.540
And he rolled a stone

05:46.540 --> 05:48.060
against the entrance of the tomb.

05:49.260 --> 05:51.540
Mary Magdalene and Mary, the mother of Joses,

05:51.780 --> 05:52.900
saw where he was laid.

